warning[W1004]: these bytes were offered to `relay` as a LEND, but `relay` keeps them past the call — so they were copied instead
 --> mem:///main.lu:5:11
  |
2 | fn relay(bs: List[int]) -> List[int] { keep(bs) }
  |          -- `bs` is declared here
  |                                             -- `bs` outlives the call here
...
5 |     relay(s.bytes()).len - 4
  |           ^^^^^^^^^ a byte view of the string's own storage; materialized to a `List[int]` here
  |
  = note: the program means what it meant; it paid one copy the lend was meant to save. If the
    copy is what you wanted, bind the bytes first — `let bs = s.bytes()` — and pass `bs`;
    that costs exactly what this call costs and says so. If it is not, the callee is the
    thing to change: a callee that only reads its parameter lends for free. A LENT view
    costs nothing and lasts only for the call. (This shape was refused as E1015 before the
    copy became the answer; that code is retired.)
